  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Identity",
      "items": [
        "users is the hub: sessions, accounts, two_factors, customer_profiles, addresses and staff_invitations hang off it.",
        "customer_profiles is 1:1 with users (its primary key is user_id).",
        "There are no roles or permissions tables: roles are a text column, users.role, and RBAC lives in code (doc/permissions.md)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Loose ends",
      "items": [
        "sessions.impersonated_by is plain text with no foreign key.",
        "verifications, rate_limits and otp_requests stand alone; otp_requests stores a phone hash and has no FK."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Reading this diagram",
      "items": [
